1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
TOP LEFT: your next action and destination. Follow the cyan marker; its distance tells you where to go.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
TOP RIGHT: breathing AIR, TOOL BATTERY and SUIT integrity. Falling reserves mean it is time to recover.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
SCAN: get close and hold E until the progress bar fills. Each observation consumes tool battery.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:34,000
LEARNING CARDS: read what the tool observed, try an explanation and review the feedback.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
LANDING CONTROLS: Space brakes, WASD steers, Enter toggles autopilot and Escape pauses.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,000
CAMPAIGN: meet the science quota, collect two observations and survey two districts before returning.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000
THRUSTER: Ctrl+Space in the air spends charge. Standing on the ground recharges this game mechanic.

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000
HAZARDS: red impact rings are a warning. These are controlled adventure scenarios, not NASA forecasts.

9
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:06,000
RECOVERY: stand near the main white shelter to refill air and battery. F1 explains unfamiliar terms.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:14,010
RETURN: press E at the habitat, choose Return to Earth, then review what your decisions achieved.

11
00:01:14,010 --> 00:01:19,020
START SIMPLE: play guided practice first. Use the Earth lab for the complete mission-design campaign.
